title: Walk_Chrysostom_GregoryOfNyssa
tags: walk
speaker: Chrysostom
---
Chrysostom: We have considered virtue, righteousness, and the good human life.
Chrysostom: Now you seek the ultimate foundation of existence itself.
Chrysostom: Our walk carries us from Values across to the Metaphysics grove.
Chrysostom: Tall pines arch overhead, filtering the quiet forest light.
Chrysostom: Moral goodness rests upon the reality God created and sustains.
Chrysostom: Gregory of Nyssa waits in the quiet clearing ahead.
Chrysostom: He contemplated divine creation, teaching how all things draw being from God.
Chrysostom: He will ask what separates genuine created reality from hollow shadow.
Chrysostom: Consider how the structure of reality grounds all true value.
Chrysostom: Let us approach his grove and explore the nature of being.
===
